# Services agreement as a compact Markdown source.
output = ARGV.len() > 0 ? ARGV[0] : "markdown-services-agreement.docx"; let body = """---
title: Service Operations Agreement
author: Harborline Devices
theme: business
toc: true
---
# Service Operations Agreement

Harborline Devices will provide Juniper Property Group with a ten-week service redesign engagement.

## Scope

- Interview six operations leads
  - Capture current intake paths
  - Identify approval delays
- Deliver a tested intake workflow
- Train the service desk

## Delivery schedule

| Phase | Deliverable | Weeks |
| :--- | :--- | ---: |
| Discover | Interviews and baseline map | 1-2 |
| Design | Prototype and service rules | 3-6 |
| Launch | Training and measurement | 7-10 |

The fixed fee is **$42,000**, invoiced at kickoff, prototype approval, and handoff. Questions may be sent through the [client portal](https://portal.example.test).

{{pagebreak}}
## Acceptance

The client will review each deliverable within five business days. Silence after that period constitutes acceptance for scheduling purposes.

{{sign: Harborline Devices}}
{{sign: Juniper Property Group}}
""";
p=_lmcode_ cli="lmoffice docx" install="github:lmctl-ai/lmoffice@latest";
let d=docx.create(${output}); d.markdown(${body}).save();
end _lmcode_
savedsl(p,output+".dslb"); r=system(concat(dsl_cli(p),["--lmcode",output+".dslb"]),120000); assert(r.code==0);
